## How long does local SEO take in Wales?

Most Welsh businesses start seeing meaningful ranking improvements within 4–8 weeks. By 3–6 months, the majority of clients are consistently appearing on page 1 for their core local search terms.

The exact timeline depends on how competitive your niche is and the current state of your website and Google Business Profile. We'll give you an honest assessment from the start.

## Frequently asked questions

**Do you offer Welsh language SEO?**

Yes. We can help businesses target both English and Welsh language search terms where relevant to your audience.

**How much does SEO in Wales cost?**

Local SEO campaigns start from around £200–£350/month depending on the scope and competition in your area. [Contact us](/contact/) for a free consultation and quote.

**Do I also need a new website?**

Not always. We can improve SEO on your existing website. But a well-built site makes SEO significantly more effective — if your current site is slow, outdated, or not mobile-friendly, a [new website](/web-design-south-wales/) is often the right first step.

**Can you guarantee rankings?**

No ethical SEO agency can guarantee specific positions. What we can guarantee is that we'll do the right things consistently, report transparently on progress, and not lock you into long contracts if results aren't there.

**What's the difference between local SEO and general SEO?**

Local SEO focuses on ranking for geographically targeted searches — "plumber in Cardiff" or "builder near Swansea". It includes Google Maps / Google Business Profile alongside website rankings. General SEO targets broader terms without a location. Most Welsh small businesses need local SEO.

